  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the thought stage, while the image carrier stays dense through the full pipeline.",
      "claim": "A persistent dense carrier, read and updated by a compact thought process.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, so spatial detail has somewhere to persist. Windows expose local token groups without replacing the carrier. The DQ-CTM thought process ticks repeatedly inside its own stage, with parameters shared across ticks. Decoding happens after the repeated thought updates, not inside the recurrence.",
